    "attributes": {
      "affiliation_basis": "STANAG 4586 Edition 3 states no affiliation field. A DLI link runs between a control station and a vehicle it controls, so FRIENDLY would usually be right \u2014 and it is an inference from deployment context, not from anything on the wire, which a relayed or recorded feed breaks. UNKNOWN, and a deployment that knows better decides it in the fusion layer where the decision is visible",
      "altitude_basis": "Altitude Type is 1 (Baro Altitude), which is not a geodetic height, so Position.alt_m is unset and the value is parked",
      "position_basis": "#4000 Inertial States fields 0101.04 and 0101.05, BAM radians to WGS-84 degrees",
      "position_source_basis": "INERTIAL, because the message carrying the position is #4000 Inertial States and the document states no GNSS source for it. Not GNSS: PositionSource is what lets a jammed-area warning discriminate, so an unstated GNSS claim would be trusted for a reason the wire never gave",
